--TEST--
`status` answers a `Core\Queue\State` and not the ordinal the row stores it as, so a program reads a state rather than a magic integer — `rule:concurrency/queue-four-members` and `rule:concurrency/attempts-are-finite-and-a-dead-letter-is-kept`, `rule:enums/closed-integer-type`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The `state` column *is* an ordinal — the enum and the column are one
// representation rather than two, which is `crate::queue`'s own module doc —
// but that is the runtime's business and not the program's. What `status`
// hands back is the closed type `rule:enums/closed-integer-type` gives an enum, so `Pending` is a name
// a program writes and `0` is never something it has to know.
var $receipt = Core\Queue::push("jobs/send-receipt.nvs");

int $wrong = Core\Queue::status($receipt);
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `int`, found `Core\Queue\State`
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
